    {
      "id": "e367054a-47f7-4e25-b612-d1af5226f74e",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -608,
        -272
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 864,
        "content": "## AI Research Radar\n\n### How it works\n\nThis scheduled workflow queries the arXiv API for recent papers, parses the XML feed, and extracts normalized paper fields. It uses an Anthropic model to score each paper for relevance, branches the scored results to both a digest path and an evaluation logging path, then summarizes the relevant papers. Finally, it aggregates the summaries into a Markdown digest and emails it via Gmail.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the Schedule Trigger with the desired run frequency.\n- Review the arXiv API query in the HTTP Request node and adjust search terms, sorting, and result limits as needed.\n- Add Anthropic credentials and verify the scoring and summarization prompts/models in the AI nodes and Scoring Config node.\n- Connect Google Sheets credentials and select the spreadsheet/sheet used by the Eval Runs node.\n- Connect Gmail credentials and configure the recipient, subject, and sender settings in the Send a message node.\n\n### Customization\n\nCustomize the scoring prompt, relevance threshold in Scoring Filter, arXiv query parameters, digest Markdown template, and evaluation fields to match your research interests and reporting needs."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "eb7b826c-ae73-4599-81bf-1bf6a1e90caf",
